      "sourceHash": "6ea00a9ea6a1b602e3d3ac013371eb8cae618df3fde8d277a0b3194288341046",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.25,
          "end": 1.97,
          "en": "Hey everyone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2,
          "end": 5.99,
          "en": "Let's talk a little bit about HTTP response code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.99,
          "end": 7.55,
          "en": "Or you can say status code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.58,
          "end": 9.65,
          "en": "Now why we need this status code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.65,
          "end": 17.84,
          "en": "Because when we will work with the API, most of the time we have to send some sort of, uh, response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.84,
          "end": 24.83,
          "en": "code or status code with the response so that in the client side, our client application can understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.86,
          "end": 27.17,
          "en": "what type of response it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.2,
          "end": 32.12,
          "en": "Now, there are several, uh, type of HTTP codes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.12,
          "end": 35.12,
          "en": "And this HTTP codes are universal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.3,
          "end": 40.52,
          "en": "It's not like it's only supported by Laravel or some other frameworks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.52,
          "end": 42.05,
          "en": "It is universal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.23,
          "end": 52.82,
          "en": "Any kind of response that you get from API endpoint will be using some sort of response code between",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 52.85,
          "end": 54.83,
          "en": "200, 400, 500.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.86,
          "end": 63.41,
          "en": "There is also another which is 300, which is not listed here Uh, but yeah, these are the most common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 63.41,
          "end": 63.92,
          "en": "one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 63.92,
          "end": 66.2,
          "en": "So level 200.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 66.23,
          "end": 70.85,
          "en": "There we have some status code like 200 by min.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 70.88,
          "end": 75.47,
          "en": "The request is okay or does mean request is a success request?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 75.5,
          "end": 78.47,
          "en": "I'm sorry, response is a success response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 78.47,
          "end": 87.44,
          "en": "So the operation that you was trying to execute with a request when it is successful, I mean the operation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 87.44,
          "end": 90.77,
          "en": "is completed successfully in the server side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 90.83,
          "end": 96.97999999999999,
          "en": "In that case, when the server will return a response, it will be A200 response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 96.97999999999999,
          "end": 100.46000000000001,
          "en": "That's mean, okay, it's been completed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 100.46000000000001,
          "end": 107.18,
          "en": "Then we have 201 as our response which is created response when we create something in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 107.18,
          "end": 110.6,
          "en": "In that case, the response code will be 201.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 111.74000000000001,
          "end": 115.88,
          "en": "If the request is accepted, it will be 2202.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 115.91,
          "end": 117.44,
          "en": "That is 203.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 117.47,
          "end": 126.86,
          "en": "Non authoritative information 404 no content Suppose you are updating a data in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 126.86,
          "end": 129.86,
          "en": "In that case you don't have to send any kind of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 131.43,
          "end": 137.22,
          "en": "information about the information, about the data that you updated in your request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 137.22,
          "end": 144.39,
          "en": "In that case, uh, we don't typically we don't send any kind of content when we update a row in the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 144.39,
          "end": 145.11,
          "en": "database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 145.35,
          "end": 150.06,
          "en": "In that case, uh, 4 to 0 four is the status code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 150.66,
          "end": 153.87,
          "en": "Then let's come into the 404, the most common one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 154.35,
          "end": 157.26,
          "en": "Uh, sorry, 4400 level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 158.43,
          "end": 161.34,
          "en": "We have 400, which is bad request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 161.67000000000002,
          "end": 163.98,
          "en": "If the request is not correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 163.98,
          "end": 167.55,
          "en": "In that case, we get bad request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 167.55,
          "end": 171.48,
          "en": "401 unauthorized, mostly common one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 171.48,
          "end": 172.38,
          "en": "In that case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 172.47,
          "end": 175.53,
          "en": "I mean, in any case, the user is not authorized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 175.53,
          "end": 183.39,
          "en": "In that case, we can return four one so that client side can understand it was an unauthorized request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 183.39,
          "end": 190.83,
          "en": "Then the forbidden if the request doesn't have the permission, in that case, we can throw 4403 uh,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 190.83,
          "end": 195.3,
          "en": "then we have 404, the most common one, and that's has been not found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 195.33,
          "end": 202.89,
          "en": "If we try to access some request sorry, API endpoint that doesn't exist, in that case it will throw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 202.89,
          "end": 204,
          "en": "us 404.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 204.03,
          "end": 206.52,
          "en": "Then we have 409 for the conflict.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 207.21,
          "end": 209.7,
          "en": "Then we have 500 level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 209.7,
          "end": 212.46,
          "en": "So it is basically server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 212.55,
          "end": 219.57,
          "en": "Uh, if if there is a anything wrong with the server, in that case this request will be thrown like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 219.57,
          "end": 221.67000000000002,
          "en": "500 mean internal server error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 221.7,
          "end": 228.3,
          "en": "If your server is not working, in that case this 500 will be thrown as a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 228.32999999999998,
          "end": 236.46,
          "en": "501 not implemented 203 bad gateway or two sorry.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 236.49,
          "end": 247.08,
          "en": "502 bad request gateway 503 service unavailable again 504 gateway timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 247.08,
          "end": 255.45,
          "en": "In case your server is not responding, you will get this, uh, code in the response for nine nine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 255.45,
          "end": 256.59,
          "en": "network timeout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 256.59,
          "end": 258.84,
          "en": "So you got the idea now?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 258.87,
          "end": 259.8,
          "en": "Not like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 260.19,
          "end": 265.89,
          "en": "We'll be using all of the status code and not like you have to memorize all of this one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 266.79,
          "end": 274.5,
          "en": "Mainly if you just remember 200201202204",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 275.34000000000003,
          "end": 281.49,
          "en": "and then let's say 404400401403.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 281.52,
          "end": 283.47,
          "en": "This one is important 404.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 283.5,
          "end": 285,
          "en": "Is totally important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 285,
          "end": 288.6,
          "en": "And we don't get 409 too much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 288.6,
          "end": 289.62,
          "en": "So yeah.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 290.15999999999997,
          "end": 299.90999999999997,
          "en": "Then 500 is important because if server server have some sort of issue, 500 will be the response 500",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 299.90999999999997,
          "end": 300.24,
          "en": "portion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 300.27,
          "end": 304.77,
          "en": "I mean level 500 is basically sent by the server by default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 304.95,
          "end": 310.29,
          "en": "Not like we have to send it when we will sending the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 310.32,
          "end": 311.7,
          "en": "This is provided by server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 311.7,
          "end": 315.78,
          "en": "So most of the time we don't have to handle the 500 request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 315.78,
          "end": 324.19,
          "en": "But in case uh, we have to handle you can just give it a read that what does what?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 324.22,
          "end": 330.28,
          "en": "Again, most of the status code will be generated automatically when you will send the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 330.28,
          "end": 335.38,
          "en": "But for make sure in most of the cases the status code is correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 335.40999999999997,
          "end": 339.34000000000003,
          "en": "We always try to type the status code with the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 339.34000000000003,
          "end": 341.59000000000003,
          "en": "It is a good practice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 342.49,
          "end": 349.27,
          "en": "Typically when in the client side, a frontend developer works with the API or API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 349.84000000000003,
          "end": 355.18,
          "en": "Always when he is getting a response, he will try to check the status code first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 355.21,
          "end": 356.83,
          "en": "What is the status code?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 356.86,
          "end": 360.61,
          "en": "Depending on the status code, you will be doing something right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 360.61,
          "end": 368.71,
          "en": "So we have to always maintain the status code when we are sending the response from the API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 368.71,
